      "message": "why are we accepting configurations with missing `Type` or non-string `Type` ?\n\nWe should not even hold these configs in memory in the first place. There is nothing we can do with them.\n\nInstead of delaying this error we can check this when configs are first parsed. `Type` is not supposed to be templated so it\u0027s not expected to change.\n\nThen an invalid config does not produce multiple repeated errors and it saves on memory usage as we won\u0027t be holding onto broken configs.",
